{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"UserPromptSubmit","additionalContext":"\n[Sutra defaults · D40 <VERSION>] Per-turn block stack — MUST emit in this order:\n\n  TOPIC-GATING FORBIDDEN. Emit the full per-turn discipline blocks for every user input,\n  regardless of topic. Personal, research, lifestyle, emotional, chitchat, greetings —\n  every input receives the same block stack. For lightweight inputs, keep block CONTENT\n  minimal (one-word fields ok) but PRESENCE is mandatory. Structure universality, not\n  depth universality. Founder direction: \"sutra for anything and everything\" (D45-cand).\n\n  1. H-SUTRA HEADER     MUST emit as FIRST line of response — literal bracketed text, NOT a skill invocation:\n                        Format: [<DIRECTION>·<VERB> · TIMING:<...> · CHANNEL:<...> · REV:<...> · RISK:<...>]\n                        On Stage-1 fail: [STAGE-1-FAIL · CLARIFY · attempt:1/1]\n  2. INPUT ROUTING      MUST emit literal block with fields: INPUT / TYPE / EXISTING HOME / ROUTE / FIT CHECK / ACTION\n  3. DEPTH + ESTIMATION MUST emit literal block with fields: TASK, DEPTH, EFFORT, COST, IMPACT\n  4. BLUEPRINT          MUST emit literal block IF tool calls planned (Edit/Write/Bash/Agent). Fields: Doing / Steps / Output looks like / Verified by / Scale / Stops if / Switch\n                        The EMITTED BLOCK IS THE CONTRACT (v3, <TS>). No marker to write: the hooks\n                        read the block in your response text. On foundational paths (charters, protocols,\n                        FOUNDER-DIRECTIONS, engine specs) blueprint-check.sh also requires a concrete\n                        \"Output looks like:\" + a runnable \"Verified by:\" (+ inline Verify: on every Step\n                        at D3+). Ordinary files are floored at Stop by per-turn-hard-gate.sh.\n  5. BUILD-LAYER marker MUST emit IF editing D38 paths (sutra/marketplace/plugin/** etc). Fields: BUILD-LAYER / ACTIVATION-SCOPE / TARGET-PATH\n                        MARKER WRITES ARE SESSION-SCOPED: write every marker file via the WRITE TOOL to\n                        .claude/sessions/<session-id>/<name> (session-id = CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID env) and\n                        include a SESSION=<session-id> line in the content. Unstamped markers are treated\n                        as legacy; never write the shared .claude/<name> path directly.\n  6. PLACEMENT          MUST emit literal one-line block (ADR-028) — every unit of work carries an address:\n                        PLACEMENT: D0 > D3 <name> > D3.D2 <name> | \"<charter title>\"\n                        Expand to the full ancestor tree ONLY when a Domain or Charter was minted this turn.\n                        The system decides the taxonomy — never ask the operator, never block on a missing\n                        domain: if nothing matches, mint under the deepest matching ancestor and continue.\n                        THEN write .claude/sessions/<session-id>/placement-registered via the WRITE TOOL\n                        (include a SESSION=<session-id> line). Enforcement is warn\n                        in this repo (promotes to HARD after 50 compliant turns).\n  7. ... tool calls (Edit / Write / Bash / Agent) ...\n  8. OUTPUT TRACE       MUST emit literal one-liner: > route: <skill> > <domain> > <nodes> > <terminal>\n\n  FLOW ACTIVATION (EVERY input, D61 amended <TS>) -- after Input Routing sets the TYPE:\n  MUST emit the FLOW block as LITERAL TEXT every turn (the way Input Routing / the H-Sutra header are\n  literal text -- NOT a Skill call). This is the firing, and it is what makes Flow as reliable as Input\n  Routing: a hook can nudge + floor a miss, but NO hook can force a Skill on the first pass. The block\n  reports the honest resolved spine for THIS unit:\n    [1] TYPE/cell  [2] FOLLOW <skill>|CONSTRUCT  [3] steps  [4] inner: lens/cynefin/factors  [5] mode  [6] close\n  Then write the flow markers (flow-classified, flow-type-resolved) via the WRITE TOOL to\n  .claude/sessions/<session-id>/<name> with a SESSION=<session-id> line (Claude Code rolls back\n  Bash writes to .claude/; unstamped markers are treated as legacy) so the floors read real state.\n  Invoke the FULL core:flow Skill (deep recursive spine) ONLY for substantive/multi-step/ambiguous work (multi_step/ambiguous_shape/unknown_how/heavy) --\n  not every trivial turn. Inline block = per-turn floor; Skill = deep mode.\n  HONESTY BAR: state what ACTUALLY resolved -- an honest 1-step ATOM block on a trivial turn is correct;\n  do NOT claim a recursive walk / cynefin / factors you did not run (that is the theater D61 forbids).\n  Floors (not the firing): flow-gate.sh (PreToolUse Edit/Write+Task) + flow-stop-check.sh (Stop, no-tool turns), HARD fleet-wide.\n\n  Conditionals (apply when triggered):\n  - Codex consult: IF Depth >= 3 with Edit/Write/MultiEdit planned → invoke core:codex-sutra skill BEFORE the Edit\n  - Skill-explain: BEFORE invoking any Skill, emit 4-line card with: SKILL / WHAT / WHY / EXPECT / ASKS\n  - Writing style (core:writing-style, HARD Stop gate writing-style-gate.sh): MINIMIZE — outcome in the first 5 prose lines, <=40 prose lines per turn (60 = one forced redo), no banned phrases, ASCII only; practices: tables_preferred_over_prose, numbers_preferred_over_adjectives, decisions_in_ascii_boxes, no_unicode_box_drawing, progress_bars_for_scores\n  - Right-effort (Karpathy): BEFORE Edit/Write, apply: think first / simpler-alt / surgical scope / verify-loop\n\n  Canonical schema: <PLUGIN>/sutra-defaults.json  (human-readable: SUTRA-DEFAULTS.md)\n  Kill-switch: touch ~/.per-turn-discipline-disabled"}}
